{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"ph2","type":"text","text":"PH2 — No auto-check, so the teacher is the “right/wrong” signal [finding]\nUnlike code, a model does not compile. Students mostly learn they are wrong when a teacher tells them.","x":1940,"y":-100,"width":380,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ph4","type":"text","text":"PH4 — A diagram survives only if someone owns it and someone reads it [finding]\nGroup ownership and a real audience decide whether modelling stays alive and careful.","x":1940,"y":541,"width":380,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ph3","type":"text","text":"PH3 — Want checks and explanations, not auto-drawn homework [finding]\nAcross tools and AI, people ask for validation and help understanding — not a machine that draws the assignment.","x":1940,"y":779,"width":380,"height":130,"color":"6"},
